meta {
  name: Register Tenant With Subscription
  type: http
  seq: 21
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/siteadmin/tenants/{{tenantId}}/register-subscription
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{siteAdminToken}}
}

docs {
  Register ONE tenant as a client on the external Subscription server
  (`POST /clients`). SiteAdmin only — requires `business:create`. No request body;
  the tenant is the `:id` path param (`{{tenantId}}`). The payload (name / address /
  contact) is built server-side from the tenant record; the subscription server keys
  the client by the tenant's `legacyTenantId ?? exchangeTenantId`.

  Idempotent: if already registered (`subscriptionRegisteredAt` set) the current
  record is returned without re-POSTing. On a fresh success the tenant's
  `subscriptionRegisteredAt` / `subscriptionClientId` / `subscriptionRegistrationMeta`
  are persisted.

  Errors:
  - 503 `SUBSCRIPTION_NOT_CONFIGURED` — SUBSCRIPTION_API_* not set.
  - 409 `SUBSCRIPTION_BUSINESS_ID_MISSING` — tenant has no legacy/exchange id.
  - 502 `SUBSCRIPTION_REGISTRATION_FAILED` — the server rejected the call.

  Returns in `data` the created/current client record (`data.original`).
}
